// ITEM 27 ΓÇö the inlet spool is a FIXED length.
  //
  // The spool carries the transition from the downcomer's base elbow to the
  // tangential inlet flange. It is sized from the pipe and the bend radius, and
  // deliberately NOT from the cyclone diameter: anchoring the cyclone to a clearance
  // that included the barrel radius made the barrel slide sideways whenever the
  // cyclone was resized, which changed the transition length, which changed the
  // solved run, which moved the downcomer. Every input tweak reshuffled the inlet.
  //
  // The cyclone's X is assigned AFTER the run is solved, below, so that the chain
  // is strictly one-directional:
