// ITEM 33 ΓÇö the exhaust stack is an equal-area round section on the fan discharge.
  // Equal area means the same mass flow at the same velocity, which is what makes it
  // a correct discharge rather than an arbitrary size.
  const downstreamStackRadiusM = Math.max(0.10, Math.sqrt(nozzleAreaM2 / Math.PI));
  // ITEM 34b ΓÇö the suction nozzle stands off far enough in Z to turn. The duct
  // approaches along -Z, so the standoff is what the final elbow has to work with.
  const idSuctionStandoffM = Math.max(
    downstreamBlowerWidthM / 2 + 0.18,
    bendRadiusM + 0.25
  );
  // ITEM 38 ΓÇö the reducer that lets the outlet duct enter the fan suction throat.
  //
  // The overhead duct is sized from the cyclone vortex finder (0.2895 m radius at the
  // IITA load, giving a 0.579 m duct) while the fan suction throat is
  // `downstreamBlowerVoluteRadiusM * 0.45` (0.2167 m, a 0.433 m opening). The duct
  // overhung the throat by 146 mm in DIAMETER: it could not enter it. Nothing bridged
  // the two, so the duct simply stopped short and left open air between itself and the
  // fan ΓÇö a separate defect from the arch, and the more literal reading of "the pipe
  // isn't fitted properly".
  //
  // Both ends are round and coaxial, so the correct transition is a concentric cone and
  // its length follows the same 1:2.5 wall rule used for the cyclone inlet transition
  // (ITEM 37).
  //
  // Capped against the straight the standoff actually leaves, not against a guessed
  // constant. The final elbow consumes `arcR` of Z and `arcR` is normally the engine bend
  // radius, so the run left into the nozzle is `idSuctionStandoffM - bendRadiusM`, which
  // the standoff guarantees is at least 0.25 m. A hard-coded 0.20 m cap was tighter than
  // the space available and forced a 1:2.2 wall on small ducts; 0.9 of the real
  // available run keeps a margin without overriding the wall rule.
  const idSuctionReducerLengthM = Math.max(
    0.06,
    Math.min(
      2.5 * Math.abs(cycloneVortexFinderRadiusM - downstreamBlowerInletRadiusM),
      Math.max(0.06, (idSuctionStandoffM - bendRadiusM) * 0.9)
    )
  );

